{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "9a5703a9-8cd8-8a40-8315-3b36948efa77",
  "created_at": "2026-02-18T10:29:22-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Conceicao Silva",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Priya Raman",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:25:43-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities Division, this is Priya. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:25:47-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning. Please, excuse me, I am calling about my water and sewer bill. It came this week and the number is very high. Too high."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:25:56-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm sorry to hear that. Can I get the service address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:26:01-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, of course. It is 323 Ocean Avenue. The name is Conceicao Silva."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:26:06-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Ms. Silva. I have the account up. The last bill does show a much higher reading than the ones before it. Do you know why that might be?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:26:17-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I know why. Please, let me explain. In December a pipe broke in the wall of the bathroom. The plumber fixed it in two days. So the water was running, yes, but it was not me using it. It is not fair that I pay like I washed a swimming pool."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:26:35-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I understand. That's what a leak adjustment is for. When a leak is repaired, the account can be reviewed and part of the excess may be adjusted. You'd need to send in the plumber's invoice showing the repair date."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:26:49-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I have the invoice. Please, tell me, where do I send it? And is it certain they will lower the bill?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:26:57-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You can drop it at the Utilities counter at City Hall, or mail it with your account number written on it. Once it's reviewed, they decide the adjustment. I can't say what it will come to, but I'll note on your account that a request is coming."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:27:13-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. And please, one more thing. On the bill it says the word consumption. Consumption, with a number. I do not know exactly this word. Can you explain it to me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:27:24-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. Consumption is just the amount of water that went through your meter during the billing period. So it's the usage, measured in units. The charge is based on that figure."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:27:35-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, so it is what the meter counted, not what I really used. Because the meter counted the pipe also."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:27:42-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Exactly. The meter can't tell the difference between a leak and a faucet. That's why the invoice matters."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:27:49-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I understand now. Please, another question. The office closes at four thirty, no? I am not always home before. Is there a way to pay by phone after four thirty? Or some other way when you are closed?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:28:02-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There's a payment drop box outside City Hall that's available after hours, and you can also pay online through the city website any time. For paying by phone, our line here is only staffed during business hours, so that part would be before four thirty."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:28:17-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. The website, I do not like it very much, but I will ask my granddaughter. The drop box I can do."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:28:25-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That works. Just put a check in with your account number on it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:28:30-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Please, excuse me, I am sorry to say, but I am tired this week. The neighbor upstairs plays the drums, at odd hours. Eleven at night, sometimes six in the morning. Then the bill. It is too much together."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:28:44-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That sounds exhausting. The drums aren't something Utilities handles, but the city's main line can point you to the right office for noise complaints. I can give you that number if you'd like."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:28:56-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, thank you, not now. First the bill. Please, do you need my telephone number for the adjustment?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:29:03-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please, in case the reviewer has a question."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:29:07-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It is 401-555-0190."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:29:09-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 401-555-0190. I've noted the account. Bring in that invoice and the review can begin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:29:15-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you very much for your patience. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T10:29:19-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too, Ms. Silva. Goodbye."
    }
  ],
